From 9a214097ab727a4c2377b26ca47190bb2dba3060 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Yu <simon011130@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:56:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(record2batch): save task uses, record batch outcomes in
 commits, and recover rollouts

Each rollout of a saved task is a task use in the task store. A use runs,
is rolled out, enters a training batch with the reports that made its
samples, and ends trained, stale_rejected, untrainable or cancelled. A
task returns to the task pool after an untrained use, until
max_task_attempts untrained uses retire it.

The trainer writes the batch's task uses and training reports to the
commit metrics and the stale consumption receipt under record2batch.
On restart, recovery reads them before records replay: a verified commit
that consumed the reports marks its uses trained, a stale receipt marks
them stale_rejected, a playing use is cancelled, and a batch whose plays
ended re-forms from the replayed reports without another rollout.
Consumed training reports with no recorded outcome stop the restart.
