+when the batch ends. When a submit fails, its tasks stay in the task pool. If
+a task's play or result save fails, the other tasks of the batch play on. The
+generic parts are ``RolloutRecord2Record`` (``reef.record2record.rollout``)
+and ``RolloutTask2Batch`` (``reef.task2batch``); any record-to-task stage that
+returns ``TaskItem`` values can feed the loop.
+
+Each rollout of a task is a task use, saved in the task store under
+``uses/``. A use runs, is rolled out with its reported episode count, enters
+a training batch with the reports that made its samples, and ends in one of
+these states:
+
+- ``trained``: the batch trained. The task does not roll out again.
+- ``stale_rejected``: the backend dropped the batch as stale.
+- ``untrainable``: the use's group was discarded or dropped before the batch
+  formed.
+- ``cancelled``: a restart interrupted the use while it played.
+
+After an untrained end, the task goes back to the task pool. After
+``max_task_attempts`` untrained uses it retires. The generator's feedback
+comes from a task's first play only. A task that retires before any play is
+reported to it as an infrastructure failure.
+
+A training commit records the batch's task uses and their training reports
+in ``metrics.record2batch``; a stale consumption receipt records them in its
+metadata. A use ends ``trained`` or ``stale_rejected`` only after that commit
+or receipt is durable. On restart, before records replay, recovery settles
+each unfinished use from this record. A commit's consumed IDs alone never
+prove that a use trained, because they also hold released and skipped
+records.
+
+- A use that a commit names, and whose reports that commit consumed, is
+  ``trained``. This includes a commit held for review: its reports never
+  replay, so the batch cannot form again. A use that a stale receipt names is ``stale_rejected``. A
+  use of such a batch that the record does not name is ``untrainable``.
+- A use that was still playing is ``cancelled``, and its task returns to the
+  task pool.
+- A batch whose plays ended, with no commit or receipt, re-forms from the
+  replayed reports without another rollout. This includes a batch whose
+  commit failed or was interrupted.
+- If a commit consumed a use's training reports but recorded no outcome for
+  its batch, recovery stops with an error rather than guess. Check the commit
+  log before restarting.
 
 When every train task of a generation has a result, the next job sends
 the generation's results to ``record_results``. A generation can therefore
